# apps.rst, irq_latency (M1): the stock path (the default).
# Schematic: 1 unit is 1 pixel; the box widths fit the labels, they are
# not durations. The masks are those of the pinned trees (both the same).
include apps.tdc
diagram irq-latency "irq_latency, stock path: edge to the time stamp in the GPIO callback"
schematic
axis "time after the edge (schematic)" -40..653

@edge
hw 76 "pin, NVIC" : The edge comes on the response pin. EXTI detects it, and the NVIC makes the interrupt pending. The pending interrupt wakes the core.
@pending anchor
idle sleep -40..pending "WFI" {primask} : The idle thread sleeps in WFI with PRIMASK set.
idle 49 "cpsie" {primask} : The idle thread clears PRIMASK (cpsie i, in k_cpu_idle()). Only then can the interrupt start.
hw 49 "entry" : Exception entry: register stacking and vector fetch. The direct and zli paths start their ISR after this step.
dev 92 "_isr_wrapper" : The wrapped path starts its ISR after this step. It does not lock interrupts.
dev 86 "GPIO driver" : The EXTI and GPIO drivers find the pin and call the user callback. They do not lock interrupts.
dev 36 "now" : The first action of the callback reads the stimulus timer: now = stim_now().
@stamp "now"
dev 43 "hist" : lat_hist_add() and lat_phase_add(), after the warm-up.
dev 82 "stim_arm()" {basepri} : Programs the next edge. The fresh counts and the compare register are written with irq_lock() (BASEPRI).
dev 43 "exit" : The ISR exit. No thread is ready, so there is no PendSV.
idle 49 "idle" {basepri} : The idle thread continues after cpsie. The idle loop: arch_irq_lock() sets BASEPRI. Then k_cpu_idle() sets PRIMASK and clears BASEPRI.
@sleeps anchor
idle sleep sleeps..653 "WFI" {primask}
span edge..stamp "irq = now - stim_edge()" !
